UPDATE companies SET description='Idahound operates from Carey, Idaho, where it was founded in 2014. The company began as a small-batch, farm-to-bowl dog food venture built on a dual commitment to pet health and environmental stewardship.

The manufacturer produces raw dog food and treats using grass-fed proteins sourced from ranches in southern Idaho. All products are custom butchered, processed, and packaged in-house, including items such as sheep and vegetable raw food, green beef tripe, raw meaty lamb neck bones, hare balls, split elk antlers, lamb crisps, and rabbit treats. Frozen orders are insulated with locally manufactured hemp wool to keep the supply chain as local as possible.

Idahound sells directly to pet owners seeking biologically appropriate raw diets for dogs and cats. Its customer base includes long-term buyers who have used the products for up to ten years, citing digestive health improvements and product quality.

The business was started to promote responsible animal husbandry, sustainable agriculture, waste and energy reduction, and the local food movement. Idahound states that its primary values are canine health and environmental sustainability, rooted in compassion for dogs, the livestock that become their food, and the planet.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom butchering", "In-house meat processing", "In-house packaging", "Raw pet food manufacturing", "Frozen order fulfillment", "Subscription management", "Direct-to-consumer shipping"], "industries": ["Pet food", "Pet supplies", "Raw pet food"], "materials": ["Grass-fed sheep", "Grass-fed beef", "Grass-fed lamb", "Rabbit", "Elk antler", "Hemp wool (insulation)", "Vegetables"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom butchering, processing, and packaging all done in-house", "Grass-fed proteins sourced exclusively from southern Idaho ranches", "Frozen shipments insulated with locally manufactured hemp wool", "Small-batch, farm-to-bowl production model", "Supply chain kept as local as possible to reduce environmental impact"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2014 -> page ''/''", "Headquarters in Carey, Idaho -> db", "Custom butchers, processes, packages in-house -> page ''/''", "Sources grass-fed proteins from southern Idaho ranches -> page ''/''", "Uses locally manufactured hemp wool for frozen order insulation -> page ''/''", "Produces raw dog food and treats (sheep, beef, lamb, rabbit, elk antler) -> page ''/''", "Sells direct to pet owners -> page ''/''", "Values: canine health, environmental sustainability, responsible animal husbandry, sustainable agriculture, waste reduction, local food movement -> page ''/'' and db description", "Small batch, farm-to-bowl model -> page ''/''", "Customer testimonials mention 10-year usage -> page ''/''"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Using grass-fed proteins fro