UPDATE companies SET description='Ideal Electric, Inc. was founded in 1994 in Winslow, Maine, and has served central Maine for over 30 years. The company operates as a licensed electrical contractor with a team of master and journeyman electricians.

The firm provides full-service electrical solutions across residential, commercial, and industrial sectors. Services include panel upgrades, new construction wiring, EV charger installations, tenant fit-outs, lighting retrofits, motor controls, high-voltage work, machine wiring, and control panel assembly. Ideal Electric also installs and services Generac whole-home standby generators and handles dedicated circuit wiring for ductless mini-split heat pump systems. The company''s crew performs troubleshooting, repairs, and scheduled maintenance for homes and businesses throughout the region.

Customers range from homeowners in Waterville and Augusta to industrial facilities in Skowhegan and Farmington. The contractor serves communities across central Maine, including Winslow, Benton, Clinton, Pittsfield, Norridgewock, and Madison. Commercial clients engage the company for maintenance contracts and fit-out projects, while industrial customers rely on its high-voltage and motor-control expertise.

Ideal Electric distinguishes itself through its licensing and insurance compliance, adherence to the National Electrical Code and Maine regulations, and a commitment to upfront pricing without hidden fees. The company holds Generac certified installer status and Efficiency Maine certification, enabling customers to access state rebates for heat pump installations. Its electricians maintain current OSHA safety training, and the firm emphasizes on-time arrival and completion on every job.', certifications=ARRAY['Maine Master Electrician License','Maine Journeyman Electrician License','Generac Certified Installer','Efficiency Maine Certified','OSHA Safety Trained']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential electrical service and installation", "Commercial electrical service and installation", "Industrial electrical service and installation", "Panel upgrades and replacements", "New construction wiring", "EV charger installation", "Tenant fit-outs", "Lighting retrofits", "Commercial maintenance contracts", "Motor controls installation and service", "High-voltage electrical work", "Machine wiring", "Control panel assembly and wiring", "Generac standby generator installation and service", "Transfer switch installation", "Load calculations for generators", "Dedicated circuit wiring for ductless mini-split heat pumps", "Ductless heat pump electrical installation and testing", "Electrical troubleshooting and repair", "Emergency service calls", "Electrical code compliance and permitting"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Generac standby generators", "Ductless mini-split heat pump systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fully licensed and insured electrical contractor in Maine", "Generac certified installer for standby generator systems", "Efficiency Maine certified for heat pump rebate eligibility", "OSHA safety trained crew", "Upfront estimates with no hidden fees"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1994 -> /about", "Headquarters in Winslow, Maine -> /about", "Services: residential, commercial, industrial electrical -> /", "Generac certified installer -> /about", "Efficiency Maine certified -> /about", "Team includes master and journeyman electricians -> /about", "Serves central Maine communities -> /about", "OSHA safety trained -> /about", "Upfront estimates, no hidden fees -> /about", "Licensed & insured -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Licensed Electrical Contractor", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ideal-electric' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Image Pointe was founded in 1977 in Waterloo, Iowa, to serve unions across America with custom-branded, union-made and USA-made apparel and promotional products. The company remains headquartered in Waterloo and operates with a fully unionized workforce organized by IUPAT District Council 81, Local 246 and Workers United Local 38.

Today, Image Pointe describes itself as the largest supplier of union and USA-made products, offering hundreds of stocked items and sourcing additional goods as needed. Its in-house art department provides custom graphic design, while production capabilities include screen printing, embroidery, and cut-and-sew manufacturing under the Dignity Apparel label—garments that are "born, built, and sewn in the USA." The combined team numbers over 150 people, with more than 80 at Image Pointe alone; average tenure runs 15 years for union graphic artists and 17 years for screen-printing and embroidery operators.

The customer base consists almost exclusively of labor unions and affiliated organizations. Testimonials on the company''s site reference the Columbus Education Association, UAW Local, and IBEW Charlotte, among others, highlighting quick turnaround, design support, and product quality for events, membership drives, and awareness campaigns.

Image Pointe says its difference lies in a mission to create "dignified, life-changing jobs" with fair wages, benefits, and safe conditions. It pledges 100 percent union labor for all graphics and production, guarantees USA-made products (union-made wherever available), and emphasizes rapid turn times and high-impact design as core commitments.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom graphic design", "Screen printing", "Embroidery", "Cut and sew manufacturing", "Union-made apparel production", "USA-made promotional products sourcing", "Rapid order fulfillment", "In-house art department"], "industries": ["Labor unions", "Promotional products"], "materials": ["USA-sourced fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% union labor for all graphics and production", "USA-made products always; union-made wherever available", "Over 80 employees with 15+ years average graphic artist experience and 17+ years average screen printing/embroidery experience", "Proudly organized by IUPAT DC 81, Local 246 and Workers United Local 38", "Mission to create dignified, life-changing jobs with fair wages and benefits"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1977 in Waterloo, Iowa -> db", "Headquarters Waterloo, Iowa -> db", "Largest supplier of union and USA-made products -> /", "Hundreds of high-quality items, sourcing anything needed -> /", "In-house art department, wide range of decoration methods -> /", "Dignity Apparel born, built, sewn in USA -> /", "Over 80 employees at Image Pointe, 150+ combined with Dignity Apparel -> /about-us", "Unionized by IUPAT DC 81 Local 246 and Workers United Local 38 -> /about-us", "15 years avg union graphic artist experience, 17 years avg screen printer/embroidery operator experience -> /about-us", "100% union labor for graphics and production -> /about-us", "USA-made always, union-made wherever available -> /about-us", "Mission to create dignified life-changing jobs with fair wages/benefits -> /about-us", "Customer testimonials: Columbus Education Association, UAW Local, IBEW Charlotte -> /", "Rapid turn times, high-impact designs, customer experience commitment -> /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All graphics and production are created by union members, for union members to advance the union cause.", "founded_year": "1977", "employee_count": "80+ at Image Pointe; 150+ combined with Dignity Apparel", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/image-pointe/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='image-pointe' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Imondi Foods is a family-owned wholesale bakery supplier headquartered in Lincoln, Rhode Island. Founded in 1984 by Tom Imondi, the company began with a pickup truck, fresh eggs, and a handshake promise to deliver reliably to local bakeries. Over four decades, it has grown into the largest family-owned bakery supply company in New England, remaining under family leadership with second-generation members Kelsey Imondi and James Lanciotti now involved in operations.

The company distributes a comprehensive range of professional baking ingredients — including flours, sugars, dairy, eggs, oils, chocolates, flavorings, mixes, and specialty items — from a 140,000-square-foot facility equipped with 20 loading docks and advanced refrigeration. An 18-truck fleet provides daily regional delivery five days a week across Rhode Island, Massachusetts, Connecticut, New Hampshire, Maine, New York, and New Jersey. The operation is SQF certified, Organic certified, and RSPO certified, with a full-time maintenance crew supporting continuous distribution.

The business was built on three core commitments: dependable service, quality products, and lasting customer relationships. Those principles, reinforced by family ownership and industry certifications, remain the foundation of its growth strategy today.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF Certified','Organic Certified','RSPO Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale bakery ingredient distribution", "Daily regional delivery (5 days/week)", "Cold storage and refrigerated warehousing", "Inventory management and order fulfillment", "Single-source wholesale supply"], "industries": ["Bakeries", "Food manufacturers", "Food service"], "materials": ["Flours", "Sugars", "Dairy products", "Eggs", "Oils", "Chocolates", "Flavorings", "Baking mixes", "Specialty baking ingredients"], "equipment": ["Refrigerated trucks", "Loading docks (20)", "Advanced refrigeration systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family owned and operated since 1984", "SQF, Organic, and RSPO certified", "18+ truck fleet delivering 5 days a week across 7 states", "140,000 sq ft facility with 20 loading docks and advanced refrigeration", "Wholesale pricing through purchasing power"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1984 by Tom Imondi -> /about", "Family-owned and operated -> /", "Headquarters in Lincoln, Rhode Island -> /", "140,000 sq ft facility with 20 loading docks and advanced refrigeration -> /about", "18+ truck fleet delivering 5 days/week across 7 states -> /", "SQF Certified, Organic Certified, RSPO Certified -> /", "Serves bakeries and food manufacturers across New England and Eastern New York -> /about", "Wholesale pricing through purchasing power -> /", "Relocated to West Warwick in 2004 -> /about", "Next generation Kelsey Imondi and James Lanciotti joined -> /about", "Tony Carmelo joined as Director of Sales in 2022 -> /about", "John Schleer joined in 2024 -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Imondi Foods supplies a comprehensive range of professional baking ingredients \u2014 including flours, sugars, dairy, eggs, oils, chocolates, flavorings, mixes, and specialty items \u2014 sourced and delivered to keep your operation running at its best.", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='imondi-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Impact Custom Apparel LLC was founded in 2005 in Cumberland, Rhode Island. The company operates from a facility on Industrial Road and serves clients throughout New England.

The shop provides custom decoration and branding services centered on a six-color screen printing press and in-house embroidery equipment. The press enables multi-color logos on garments for uniforms, giveaways, and fundraisers, while embroidery adds a classic finish to personalized items. It also produces large-format graphics for vehicle wraps, vinyl banners, and frontage signs, and sources a wide range of promotional products. Additional offerings include graphic design, branding strategy, and the creation of online company stores for items such as business cards, letterhead, and yard signs.

Clients range from non-profit organizations like the East Bay Food Pantry & Thrift Shop to schools, Greek-life groups, and businesses seeking uniforms, giveaways, or fundraising merchandise. The company has positioned itself as a regional source for both decorated apparel and branded signage, describing itself since 2005 as New England''s source for apparel and promotional items.

