UPDATE companies SET description='Intelligent Manufacturing Solutions (IMS) was founded in 2005 in Londonderry, New Hampshire, to fill a market gap for high-quality rapid prototype and small-lot printed circuit board assembly. The company was acquired by Perimeter Solutions (NYSE: PRM) on December 24, 2024, broadening its portfolio to include acquisition and sustainment of OEM legacy product lines.

IMS provides full life-cycle electronics assembly services, spanning quick-turn prototypes, high-mix low-volume production, box build, design-for-manufacturability analysis, and end-of-life support including IP acquisition. The New England facility operates multiple SMT lines with Mycronic pick-and-place machines, Heller reflow ovens, 3D AOI and X-ray inspection, selective and wave soldering, and aqueous cleaning. The company emphasizes rapid turnaround, shipping prototypes overnight anywhere in the United States and delivering tested assemblies within hours for short-notice orders.

IMS serves aerospace and defense, medical and instrumentation, communications, consumer electronics and IoT, automotive, and industrial sectors. Reference customers include an automotive technology company, a consumer robotics company, and an IoT solutions provider, all citing the firm''s speed, quality, and flexibility in moving from prototype to full box build.

The business was purpose-built to address the lack of responsive service for complex, low-volume PCBA projects. Management, with over 25 years of shared EMS experience, focuses on minimizing time-to-market and mitigating excess and obsolete inventory charges. The Perimeter Solutions acquisition adds a model for acquiring and sustaining OEM non-core products through their remaining lifecycle.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rapid prototype PCB assembly", "Box build assembly", "High-mix low-volume PCB assembly", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) analysis", "End-of-life product support", "IP acquisition and legacy product sustainment", "Short-notice production", "Build-to-order manufacturing", "Component sourcing and procurement", "SMT pick-and-place assembly", "Through-hole assembly", "Selective soldering", "Wave soldering", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "3D X-ray inspection", "Solder paste inspection (SPI)", "BGA/LGA/QFN placement", "Rework and repair", "Aqueous cleaning", "Stencil cleaning", "Programming and labeling", "Packaging and fulfillment"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Medical & Instrumentation", "Communications", "Consumer Electronics/IoT", "Automotive", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Mycronic MY300 SX14 pick-and-place (30,000 cph)", "Mycronic M100 SX14 pick-and-place (25,000 cph) (2 units)", "Mycronic MY9E pick-and-place (15,000 cph)", "Heller 1808 MkIII reflow oven (3 units)", "Mycronic Primo 3D solder paste inspection", "Mycronic MY600 deposition with vision and repair", "Mycronic My500 deposition with vision and repair", "SpeedPrint SP710 advanced vision intelligence (2 units)", "MPM Accuflex dual system", "UniComp AX8200 programmable X-ray 2D/3D modeling 130kV", "Mirtec MV6 Omni 3D AOI (2 units)", "VJ Electronics Summit 1100HR rework", "VJ Electronics Summit 1800HRE rework", "Nordson Novo 103 selective soldering with pre-heat (Pb-free)", "Ace 102 selective soldering with pre-heat (Pb)", 