UPDATE companies SET description='International Wire is headquartered in Camden, New York. The company describes itself as the largest non-vertically integrated manufacturer of copper and copper-alloy wire products in the United States. No founding year or ownership details are disclosed in the available information.

The company produces a comprehensive range of wire products including bare copper wire, tinned copper wire, tinned copper tubular and flat braids, and stainless steel tubular braids. Its capabilities span wire drawing, conductor fabrication, and custom wire solutions, with single-end wires available from 44 AWG to 2 AWG, stranded wires for electronics and cable assemblies, and braided wires for RFI/EMI shielding. The firm notes it offers thousands of products and serves customers across the United States and Europe.

International Wire serves markets including advanced manufacturing and automation, electrification and power infrastructure, aerospace and defense systems, data centers and critical connectivity, transportation and e-mobility, smart living and appliances, energy extraction and processing, healthcare and medical devices, and built environment and infrastructure. Specific applications cited range from robotics and factory automation to solar farms, wind turbines, nuclear energy, in-flight entertainment and cabin management systems, 5G networks, electric vehicles, home appliances, oil and gas operations, medical devices, and building wiring and grounding.

The company states its mission is to deliver value-driven, high-quality wire products and services that exceed client expectations, guided by core values of safety, people, customers, products and services, conduct, and continuous improvement. It emphasizes decades of experience in wire drawing, conductor fabrication, and custom wire solutions as a foundation for its offerings.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire drawing", "Conductor fabrication", "Custom wire solutions", "Single-end wire manufacturing (44 AWG to 2 AWG)", "Stranded wire manufacturing", "Braided wire manufacturing (tubular and flat)", "Tinning", "Braiding", "RFI/EMI shielding"], "industries": ["Advanced Manufacturing & Automation", "Electrification & Power Infrastructure", "Aerospace & Defense Systems", "Data Centers & Critical Connectivity", "Transportation & e-Mobility", "Smart Living & Appliances", "Energy Extraction & Processing", "Healthcare & Medical Devices", "Built Environment & Infrastructure", "Renewable Energy"], "materials": ["Copper", "Copper alloys", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest non-vertically integrated manufacturer of copper and copper-alloy wire products in the U.S.", "Decades of experience in wire drawing, conductor fabrication, and custom wire solutions", "Comprehensive product range: bare and tinned copper wires, tinned and stainless steel braids", "Serves customers across the United States and Europe"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Camden, New York -> db", "Largest non-vertically integrated manufacturer of copper and copper-alloy wire products in the U.S. -> db", "Offers bare copper wire, tinned copper wire, tinned copper tubular braids, tinned copper flat braids, stainless steel tubular braids -> /", "Single-end wire range 44 AWG to 2 AWG -> /", "Stranded wire for electronics and cable assemblies -> /", "Braided wire for RFI/EMI shielding -> /", "Wire drawing, conduct