UPDATE companies SET description='Ironwood Mills was founded in 2016 in Phoenix, Arizona, by Scott Mills. After more than two decades as an independent contractor across various trades, Mills turned a lifelong passion for woodworking and a self-described "urban lumberjack" pursuit into a dedicated shop. The business began with a focus on rescuing discarded trees from the Phoenix area and transforming them into custom furniture and live-edge slabs.

The company produces handcrafted furniture, hardwood slabs, and dimensional lumber from locally sourced Arizona species such as mesquite, olive, and ash. Its 8,342 North 7th Street facility houses a Lucas Mill 10-30 capable of cutting logs up to five feet in diameter and 21 feet long, a Wood-Mizer bandsaw mill for smaller logs, a Wood Wizz surfacing machine that handles pieces up to 7 by 17 feet, and an iDRY vacuum kiln for controlled drying. Services include custom milling at $150 per hour (one-hour minimum), machine surfacing at $150 per hour, and vacuum kiln drying at $2 per board foot with a 1,000-board-foot minimum.

Ironwood Mills serves three primary customer groups: designers and architects seeking unique material palettes for projects, woodworkers and makers who need milling, surfacing, or drying services for their own stock, and homeowners commissioning one-of-a-kind tables, bases, and specialty pieces. The shop also offers team-building workshops and sells surfaced slabs directly through its online store.

The founder’s background in diverse construction trades and a deep appreciation for desert ecology drive the company’s emphasis on urban lumber reclamation. Mills describes the work as a privilege to “take a forgotten & unwanted tree and bring it back to life,” a philosophy that extends to the shop’s policy of assessing each log individually and refusing to refinish existing furniture.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and fabrication", "Live-edge slab production", "Log milling (Lucas Mill 10-30, up to 5'' dia x 21'' long)", "Dimensional lumber milling (up to 10x10, Wood-Mizer bandsaw)", "Machine surfacing (Wood Wizz, up to 7'' x 17'')", "Vacuum kiln drying (iDRY, min 1000 BF)", "Hardwood slab sales (online and in-person)", "Table base fabrication", "Team-building workshops"], "industries": ["Designers & Architects", "Woodworkers", "Homeowners"], "materials": ["Acacia", "Ash", "Carob", "Chinaberry", "Cork Bark Oak", "Elm", "Eucalyptus", "Ficus", "Hickory", "Indian Rosewood", "Juniper", "Mesquite", "Olive", "Pine", "Silk Oak", "Sycamore"], "equipment": ["Lucas Mill 10-30", "Wood-Mizer bandsaw mill", "Wood Wizz surfacing machine", "iDRY vacuum kiln"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Urban lumber reclamation: rescuing discarded Phoenix-area trees for furniture and slabs", "Lucas Mill 10-30 cuts logs up to 5'' diameter and 21'' length", "iDRY vacuum kiln provides precise, uniform drying at lower temperatures", "Wood Wizz surfaces slabs up to 7'' x 17'' without tear or burn marks", "Custom furniture and live-edge slabs from 16+ Arizona hardwood species"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2016 -> db", "Headquarters Phoenix, AZ -> db and /about page", "Founder Scott Mills -> /about page", "Team members Kit Vander Jagt and Michael Toret -> /about page", "Services: custom furniture, urban lumber, milling, machine surfacing, kiln drying -> / and /services pages", "Equipment: Lucas Mill 10-30, Wood-Mizer bandsaw, Wood Wizz, iDRY vacuum kiln -> /services page", "Milling capacity: up to 5'' diameter, 21'' long; dimensional up to 10x10 -> /services page", "Surfacing capacity: up to 7'' x 17'' -> /services page", "Kiln drying: minimum 1000 board feet, $2/BF -> /services page", "Milling rate: $150/hr, 1 hour minimum -> /services page", "Surfacing rate: $150/hr -> /services page", "Industries served: Designers & Architects, Woodworkers, Homeowners -> / and /about pages", "Materials: 16 Arizona hardwood species listed -> / page", "Business address: 8342 N 7th Street, Phoenix, AZ 85020 -> / page", "Business hours: Mon-Fri 8am-4pm, Sat 8am-2pm -> / page"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We transform locally sourced Arizona hardwoods into custom furniture that inspires creativity and connection", "founded_year": "2016", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "Milling: 1 hour minimum ($150/hr); Kiln drying: 1,000 board feet minimum ($2/BF)", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ironwood-mills' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
